  "meta": {
    "title": "2026-06-09-post-mortem-visuals · candidate-009 (placeRect-per-rect)"
  },
  "agent": {
    "note": "Iter 9 — refactored authoring per your guidance: each rect placed via placeRect (singular), then chained via addOverlayLayer. One rendered frame per layer, so input rects map 1:1 to output stableKeys regardless of heights or alignment — no band-split footgun. Masks attach exactly to the 4 avatar frames; nothing leaks. Same colors + dims as the iter7 attempt that broke (40×40 circle avatars, 600×100 bubbles, brand orange human, dark agent, full-width system, #14151b bg). Lesson for the agent: placeRects is for batched packing with optimized layer count; placeRect+addOverlayLayer is for safe one-at-a-time placement where each rect is independent. The new circleMask helper kept the avatar mask path one-liner — bounds=40×40 matches the rect, no stretching.",
    "question": "Layout should now match what we agreed on at iter6 with the iter7 color palette. Open with Rects + Masks + Label colors all on. If the visual is right, next direction: should we (a) wire this layout into the actual post-mortem template chat-stream, or (b) keep iterating in sandbox first (e.g. add the timestamp / status row, scrollback behavior preview)?",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "known",
        "value": "color-palette-exploration"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "refine",
        "summary": "placeRect-per-rect authoring — same Y bounds no longer a constraint"
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "008"
      },
      "layoutIntent": "free"
    },
    "response": {
      "body": "Good result. Lets slightly reduce the intensity of both the orange and gray colors",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-10T04:05:03.343Z"
    }
  },
